      "message": "[error] Line 1892: 🔴 `pjsip_msg_body_create` is fed with `pj_str_t content` pointing to `sdp.data()` from a function parameter (`answerMediaChangeRequestWithExternalSdp`). That buffer lifetime ends when the function returns, but PJSIP message body keeps a pointer, which can cause use-after-free/corrupted SDP on async send. Build the body from storage that outlives the send (e.g., `externalSdp_` after assignment) or duplicate into `tdata-\u003epool` (e.g., `pj_strdup*`) before assigning `tdata-\u003emsg-\u003ebody`.",
